Undo the last commit but keep changes staged
git reset --soft HEAD~1
The commit is removed.
Your changes stay in the staging area (ready to commit again).



Undo the last commit and move changes back to working area (unstaged)
git reset HEAD~1
git reset HEAD~2

The commit is removed.
Your changes are now in the working area, so you can edit them freely.


Undo the last commit and discard changes completely (dangerous)
git reset --hard HEAD~1
The commit is removed.

All changes are lost permanently.
